            <ArticleTitle>[Formation of the marginal &quot;pro-oxidant&quot; zone and its role in the enhancement of lipid peroxidation in the area of myocardial ischemia and infarction].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>538-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The formation of peripheral zone devoid of dehydrogenase activity but possessing vessels connected with the normal myocardium was demonstrated in the area of fresh myocardial infarction 2 h after coronary occlusion. A direct correlation between the changes of the zone area and the intensity of free radical lipid peroxidation in the area of fresh myocardial infarction was established.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
